            <div id="document"><h2>e is Irrational&nbsp;</h2>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem: </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;e is irrational&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__text"> is irrational</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><strong>Proof:</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p>We will prove this theorem by contradiction. Therefore,&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;assume e is rational&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">assume </span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__text"> is rational</span></span></span></span></span>. That is, &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;e=m/n ,1 leq n for some m,n in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Utilizing the facts that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n!=(n-1)!*n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.72777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n*(m/n)=m&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.686em; height: 1.6165600000000002em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size2">(</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size2">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by algebra&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by algebra</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n!*e=n!*(m/n)\n=((n-1)!*n)*(m/n)\n=(n-1)!*(n*(m/n))\n=(n-1)!*m&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 4.06em;"><span style="top: -6.05em;"><span style="height: 2.14em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 4.06em;"><span style="top: -6.05em;"><span style="height: 2.14em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.686em; height: 1.6165600000000002em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size2">(</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size2">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.91em;"><span style="height: 2.14em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.25em; height: 1em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.72777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.686em; height: 1.6165600000000002em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size2">(</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size2">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -1.78em;"><span style="height: 2.14em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.72777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.686em; height: 1.8359999999999999em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size2">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.686em; height: 1.6165600000000002em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size2">(</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size2">)</span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size2">)</span></span></span></span><span style="top: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 1.2em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.72777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Therefore, we have shown that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n!*e=(n-1)!*m&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.72777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span></span>. Recall that &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;1 \\leq n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>. Since <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq 1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by arithmetic&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by arithmetic</span></span></span></span></span>, it follows from the transitivity of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\leq&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;that&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp; and therefore&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>. We know that,&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;1 in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp; Since both 1 and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span> are natural,&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n-1 in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> by the definition of an integer.&nbsp;Further, we already know that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;1 leq n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp; since <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span> is natural and positive. Therefore, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;1-1 leq n-1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span> by translation. And since <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;1-1=0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by arithmetic&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by arithmetic</span></span></span></span></span>, this simplifies to <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 leq n-1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&le;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span>. It follows that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(n-1)! in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.72777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>. Further, since the product of integers are integers (recall <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;m \\in \\mathbb{Z}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> by assumption),&nbsp;we know that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(n-1)! * m in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.72777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp; Recall from the transitive chain above that&nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;(n-1)! \\cdot m=n! \\cdot e&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">&minus;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1)!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span></span></span></span></span>. Thus,&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n!*e in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;by substitution&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text"> by substitution</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Using the definition of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;e&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">e</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n!*e=n!*(sum k=0 to infinity of 1/k!)\n=n!*(sum k=0 to n 1/k!+sum k=n+1 to infinity of 1/k!)\n=n!*(sum k=0 to n of 1/k!) + n!*(sum k=n+1 to infinity of 1/k!)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mtable"><span class="col-align-r"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 5.19em;"><span style="top: -7.18em;"><span style="height: 3.36em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="col-align-l"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 5.19em;"><span style="top: -7.18em;"><span style="height: 3.36em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span><span class="ML__cmr">&sdot;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -1.302113em; height: 2.9535100000000005em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size4">(</span><span class="ML__op-group"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.66em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -1.84em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">=0</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.05em;"><span style="height: 1.61em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__op-symbol ML__large-op">&sum;</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -4.3em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="